# Spiral similarity lemma — if AB and CD meet at X, the second intersection M of circles (XAC) and (XBD) is the center of the spiral similarity mapping A→C, B→D, so MA/MC = MB/MD (source: Evan Chen, EGMO)
A B C = triangle
D = free
X = meet(line(A, B), line(C, D))
M = meet(circumcircle(X, A, C), circumcircle(X, B, D))
prove eqratio(M, A, M, C, M, B, M, D)
